#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:5
#: 5a1dbfa34829444dbd72a761bd33231a
msgid "Archived: Advanced MultiCopter Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:7
#: bab58761ce0a449d91e37075b3750c75
msgid ""
"This section is topics related to advanced multicopter construction and "
"design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:12
#: 1b7aa7da037d4e2bbed0d8fbb76f1b5e
msgid ""
"For information on understanding how a multicopter works please go "
":ref:`Here <what-is-a-multicopter-and-how-does-it-work>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:14
#: 8f68984b67a640ea8c9551faee6fdeb1
msgid ""
"For information on how to build your own simple Quadcopter using kits or "
"frames go :ref:`Here <build-your-own-multicopter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:16
#: 1b98922541e344a888f834725de83231
msgid ""
"For information on building or setting up a copter for first Person View "
"(FPV) go :ref:`Here <common-fpv-first-person-view>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:20
#: a19efaba74f44e688ef0241ed5ccdc58
msgid "There are several popular frame layouts for MultiCopters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:22
#: 476097a56e774328b1ae68f59e6421d1
msgid ""
"The Tricopter uses 3 motor / propeller propulsion units with a servo to "
"rotate one of them to compensate for adverse yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:25
#: 0988ce5974f34a87a5e43c461a22fc6a
msgid ""
"Tricopters were popular early on when the brushless motor / propeller "
"units were new and scarce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:27
#: a24dd52f13bd41ab8ed7703ff30c165a
msgid ""
"They suffer from less than stellar performance and do not scale well to "
"larger sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:29
#: 057e2842b39448a8b36de9cad14135e3
msgid ""
"But they still have some popularity for small, light hobby use "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:31
#: ecbab07822f344928dcb06237113f0b9
msgid ""
"Because this is primarily an outdated design we will not expand further "
"on it in this article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:37
#: 3538b05c124049bebd1095a088b7fad3
msgid ""
"The very popular Quadcopter has 4 motor/propeller units and is available "
"in any size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:40
#: ae8357d732d445d193f638f873531dd7
msgid ""
"A Quadcopter is an elegantly simple design and is hands down the most "
"popular layout for a whole lot of reasons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:42
#: 528521401d6c4ff0b5080719a445650b
msgid ""
"Quadcopters are symmetrical and embody the simplest principle of "
"operation for controlling roll, pitch, yaw and motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:44
#: 7d32448cc9374e65b1c39a29eb9d55a0
msgid ""
"Simply varying the speed of each of the motors provides full 3D motion "
"and rotation and hover capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:46
#: 4de095e539454eba8f319e195c87da91
msgid ""
"They are relatively inexpensive to produce and they scale well to "
"production manufacturing techniques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:48
#: 47c2664f280840908e866776d70cb6f1
msgid ""
"In various sizes and layouts they are capable of actually performing "
"useful tasks beyond simply flying around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:50
#: 4ebb3f3582984fd8816b2b0c057ca0a1
msgid ""
"Their primary drawback is that a single motor failure generally results "
"in an abrupt descent to the ground (crash)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:52
#: e055924e0fd24fe59355e3aeb6e53f93
msgid ""
"A very wide variety of materials and techniques can be employed to "
"produce a useful Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:54
#: 2eeea30c95bd49f68e06fd7181961569
msgid "There are several popular configurations for QuadCopters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:56
#: 68aaa115dce14b4ca57de037c5684453
msgid ""
"X with and X frame arm layout and the front and back of the copter "
"between 2 propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:58
#: 11f3b5a165384ae9aba7d53d30967431
msgid ""
"and with the same kind of X frame layout as above but with the front and "
"back of the copter in line with one of the propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:61
#: 2a5093854bda471a957335a93fad89c2
msgid ""
"\"Dead Cat\" a variation on X which in which the frame arms are further "
"apart in the front and the back than they are side to side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:65
#: d8dfaa3cfe45418998a559228432d145
msgid ""
"Name actually comes from Bart Jansen a Dutch artist who stuffed his "
"expired cat and made a Quadcopter out of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:68
#: 8add44ee96d14824941d13670060716e
msgid ""
"H which has frame side arms running between the motors on each side and "
"connected with one or more frame arms in the middle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:70
#: e676ea07ca704852b4e17169b6039132
msgid ""
"Square which has frame arms connecting between motors (and usually "
"intermediate frame arms supporting a central frame.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:72
#: c98e9a933d5f4752b82bbb9beb7e8077
msgid "And variations including ones with the motors laid out on a circle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:74
#: c904e4dbd3e84e589ffc24f52094e514
msgid ""
"Most of them primarily operate the same as the X frame (provides better "
"camera exposure between motors among other things)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:77
#: 354660b5c23543debe7ce2ab1133757c
msgid ""
"I recommend the standard X frame design because it is strong and simple "
"and its natural symmetry balances flying forces better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:81
#: f1dc56a5c4cd42049839a035e4528b99
msgid ""
"A humming bird sized `Estes Proto X <http://www.estesrockets.com/helis-"
"quads/quadcopters/004606-proto-x>`__ is shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:88
#: 60c49da8a4f749db939874b0d9db4c08
msgid ""
"A fifteen thousand dollar SteadyDrone Q4D-X Quadcopter with 28\" "
"propellers, 8KG lifting capability and claimed 60 minute flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:95
#: 61ce172d05e246b1b199a677baf10ea9
msgid ""
"For professional use, HexaCopters and OctoCopters with 6 and 8 "
"Motor/propeller propulsion units are popular."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:98
#: 7b0492e58792468fbc402517922948c3
msgid ""
"Hexacopters, Octocopters, Hex Y's and Octo X's can provide stable heavy "
"lift platforms good for photography and other uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:100
#: a9bdbaf9520747bcab10540e7ec4b2c8
msgid ""
"Hex and Octocopters may have the benefit of potentially being able to "
"continue to fly with a single motor failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:102
#: 2cd70ad1f63a410490deb29a545e6d08
msgid ""
"However the increased complexity versus a Quadcopter makes them more "
"failure prone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:104
#: dac565daf836434a8005ed95ca9559fc
msgid ""
"The reduction in prop size and increase in prop speed result in a "
"smoother flight than an equivalent large blade Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:106
#: 40f9fe9498a3481688ec91ef8666cc12
msgid ""
"However it also results in some reduction in flight efficiency and "
"endurance all other things being equal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:112
#: a09be16c7fa64b3a80a53ceaf65efadc
msgid ""
"Hex Y6 and Octo X8 designs with pairs of coaxial motor/propeller units "
"mounted back to back are also becoming popular."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:114
#: 6bde153ed08642b69d22a313a05d2dc0
msgid ""
"Singlecopters and Coax copters are very new designs and have some "
"advantages in specific applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:117
#: 92d8258929bb4175bdeea36dc4c1b603
msgid ""
"Since they tend to a single ducted body for either the one or two "
"motor/propeller units they tend to be self protected indoors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:119
#: fc0371445f23494dbee5910c838f6900
msgid ""
"The coax copter which relies on variable thrust on each of its 2 props "
"for rotation is functionally simpler than the single copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:121
#: 439a6daa601f49fb8a9ee5279efa577a
msgid ""
"The side profile of the ducted body makes these copters more susceptible "
"to winds outdoors requiring more effort to compensate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:123
#: decc5fa5dff249cd84bb218c07198c7f
msgid ""
"While generally good at hovering and fine positioning, they are more "
"speed and performance limited than other multicopter designs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:125
#: f518100fe96341b2b5059b4c95aa0abd
msgid ""
"The Singlecopter in particular is reasonably adaptable to gasoline "
"engines for much greater endurance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:127
#: a4c8998b528543bbbc54ff99fa4ed0c2
msgid ""
"The possibility of using a single large propeller implies that good "
"efficiencies could be realized even with an electric versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:130
#: 5688882e901d4a4aa3f8fb3aaa8e948f
msgid ""
"The Singlecopter features a single motor/propeller unit with 4 servo "
"controlled vanes to direct roll, pitch and yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:136
#: c8ea7a7fca2043e39e3291065dfa6901
msgid ""
"The Coaxcopter has dual motor/propeller units for thrust and yaw control "
"and 2 servo controlled vanes for roll and  pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:142
#: f320a653bc48484eba0bbc538bbf56ce
msgid ""
"There are also variable pitch Multicopters for incredible acrobatic "
"performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:145
#: 3114375c925f40c98f09e16a0b9ca206
msgid ""
"Variable pitch multicopters have some interesting potential uses as well "
"like the `Curtis Youngblood Stingray 500 "
"<http://curtisyoungblood.com/V2/products/quadcopters/stingray-500>`__ "
"shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:147
#: c54e15244ac745b6b47a0bf7089e08ca
msgid ""
"Servo control of the props (rotors) produces roll, pitch and yaw so they "
"are often powered by a single motor with shaft or belt drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:150
#: 7a67c2068d2b409fab561f83308e13ec
msgid ""
"If you use a single motor it is feasible to use a gasoline engine giving "
"you the potential for considerable endurance and range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:152
#: e6b12e82a5f8463db7ebdaab9f9737fb
msgid ""
"These are very high performance and can even fly inverted, they are also "
"mechanically more complex but can be built robustly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:158
#: 05c91f321cd2470494052640fd65b9c0
msgid ""
"And copters with more than 8 motor/propeller units may be useful for "
"specialized, extreme `(or insane) "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L75ESD9PBOw>`__ applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:166
#: c031516fcb3f4ec7b5346b145358e23f
msgid "Motors, propellers and ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:168
#: 8bbeeedbcab44bde8b64109906b85f25
msgid ""
"For multicopters, motors, propellers and ESCs (speed controllers) are "
"critical and have been failure prone in the past."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:171
#: c034500714ee40838cafd91a6c8acd91
msgid ""
"This ECalc based `Xcopter: motor - propeller - battery - ESC calculator "
"<https://www.ecalc.ch/xcoptercalc.php?ecalc&lang=en>`__ will help you "
"pick the best components for your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:174
#: dc110a793c2d4828a6c7f642725b05b9
msgid ""
"Quadcopter design will be used for illustration as they are the most wide"
" spread and the most versatile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:177
#: 4aa90864f28f4aaa9d8f47dea8c6f417
msgid ""
"But the information applies equally to Hex and Octo designs, either "
"conventional or coaxial Y and X types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:180
#: 92f62551358948fcb2322cea67977b38
msgid ""
"The brushless out-runner motors have to support the full weight of the "
"copter continuously while turning at high speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:183
#: 90b4746faabd448bbc5a98a68f9336b1
msgid ""
"Hobby grade motors have often used inadequate Conrad type unsealed "
"bearings which are good axially but not in thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:186
#: f9206e5d553345fdb033649a09e9a7c4
msgid ""
"And the motors are usually open frame to permit the greatest cooling but "
"providing little or no protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:188
#: 3c3ec996e3e248e58f9829038aab0c3e
msgid ""
"This has meant an unnecessarily high failure rate and very poor survival "
"in wet or dusty conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:190
#: 4442e93b7f124476a6f8f9e2ead766fb
msgid ""
"The cheapest possible Chinese motor is never a good choice for something "
"that literally hangs in the air by its motor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:193
#: f073343eebcb4ccdb9aee509aac5acb7
msgid ""
"Some of the best motors have 2 or better 3 easily replaceable ABEC-7 "
"bearings, RCTiger-Motor Pro series and KDE for instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:196
#: 6fbbafd05034439c82d60a44bd758f88
msgid ""
"The best motors are well ventilated, made with high temperature "
"components and coated and sealed for environmental protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:198
#: 3cefb68219af4991a87884ba21695b6b
msgid ""
"The best motors like TMotor and KDE have performance comparison charts, "
"these should be reviewed when designing a copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:200
#: 3d74016ac41742da9f973511535cf60b
#, python-format
msgid ""
"You are best off selecting motor - prop - battery cell combinations that "
"will provide 10% or higher G/W efficiency at 50% throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:203
#: e87bac873c4643438c87bcfb24fdd6fd
msgid ""
"You should also target you copter design weight so that it hovers at "
"approximately 50% throttle for optimum efficiency and flight time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:206
#: da6adcaeef26477cb20e64eac4821338
msgid ""
"Top motors can cost considerably more, but reliability, performance and "
"efficiency can be much better and worth it in the long run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:209
#: 658415879c8d45a7b5b9eb0a2bba0afa
msgid ""
"Low KV motors running on lower voltage (fewer cells) with large "
"propellers are the most efficient and provide the longest flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:213
#: f86b114387f84ab8b124b14670aec0da
msgid ""
"Selecting the best motor, propeller, battery set will enable you to build"
" a copter with a usable 30 minute flight time including a camera."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:217
#: 06efc7fd8cd7449dbcf891a6ec83a1a5
msgid ""
"You can get 30 minutes from 330 copters with 8\" props to 700 size "
"copters with 18\" props depending on camera / gimbal weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:220
#: 82e303c4e3844b278ae383d99dc20ea9
msgid ""
"It is very hard to get much more than 30 minutes of usable flight time "
"from any \"useful\" multicopter regardless of size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:222
#: 2585431a69f645eba15af4edc7794f97
msgid ""
"For hobby grade components, 20 minute maximum flight times would be a "
"more realistic goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:225
#: f9202d7d75c042b6b2720a6e03d614c7
msgid "ESCs are also very important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:227
#: a6786bbdce1349b4a1c699a72f3a926c
msgid "High quality ESCs are more reliable than cheap ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:228
#: a5dbb03de768459eb87d5128f6bda2d6
msgid ""
"And ESCs need to be properly sized to ensure they can provide the maximum"
" current that is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:231
#: c22132d5fc814f50b47bb227293393ba
msgid ""
"Generally use the right size not over sized because they are more "
"efficient if operated in the appropriate range (and lighter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:235
#: 369e73202b5c46efb53d19d462284b50
msgid ""
"Sufficient cooling is also very important especially for \"Heavy Lift\" "
"copters, and the ESCs may need to be placed in the air stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:238
#: ffe1510d65e2458583d1cde8784b246a
msgid ""
"For small to medium QuadCopters there are four in one ESCs in the 20 - 30"
" Amp size range with several advantages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:241
#: 9a40be69bc7444db9a0c7bb698a0bcd9
msgid ""
"They eliminate the need for a power distribution plate or block and all "
"the attendant wiring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:243
#: b560f5a848004429933473904865264a
msgid ""
"The considerable reduction in DC wiring results in less DC EMF radiation "
"interference with the compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:245
#: 1f3836b20af54fca9e97eb6c998467c4
msgid ""
"They can often be conveniently installed tidily in the center of the "
"copter frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:247
#: b1020661fbe84dd5952f8035ffe12a0d
msgid ""
"The 20 and 25 amp ones work with 3 or 4 cell LiPo batteries and the 30 "
"amp one works with 3 to 6 cell batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:249
#: ba2d6a6f71db40b1aa3a202b7e86dc57
msgid ""
"They have a built in aluminum heat sink plate on one side (which you can "
"augment with a finned heat sink if necessary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:251
#: ec76a85cece84484b2077017a42ad23b
msgid ""
"You can use a thin layer of Fujik silicone thermal glue to attach a "
"finned heat sink if one is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:253
#: cbcb5f31d6324b01b1a2e088f5724abf
msgid ""
"They generally have higher reliability than individual ESCs and are "
"reasonably priced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:256
#: 71e485a2ac9d4b14bd902084a7864760
msgid ""
"Larger diameter slower turning propellers are normally a lot more "
"efficient than smaller, faster ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:259
#: 3d4bb8e896a446afb98b15198e62c651
msgid "But there are limits and drawbacks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:261
#: 4183e1a03e0b40ea96eb8d3645a6f265
msgid ""
"Trying to turn too large a prop for a given motor can cause it to "
"overheat so motors usually have a maximum prop size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:263
#: 0ac937db4c7847dc871fc040ec917522
msgid ""
"Also, really large, slow props can reduce the responsiveness of the "
"multicopter and even cause it to oscillate in the air or vibrate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:266
#: 1d08f2b4bb39446386f036e48be920be
msgid ""
"Unless taken to extremes these difficulties are not usually significant "
"and can be compensated for by various means."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:268
#: 837b9533f69e49799163d6d078aa2887
msgid ""
"And you can always drop the diameter an inch if the handling "
"characteristics or motor stress are not what you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:271
#: ec22589a6118436081c815b6a82c39ba
msgid ""
"There are also different designs of propellers and for larger ones "
"turning at slower speeds design is especially critical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:274
#: 6e869074325040dc9876a4b45cd54b2d
msgid ""
"Carbon fiber designs with cupped blades that are wider at the hub and "
"narrower at the tip are best for larger sizes 14\" and over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:277
#: 85c56fa8a75b43ae8247e6e044697c7b
msgid ""
"Smaller ones in the 14\" and under category can be of more conventional "
"design with a wider than normal blade and of plastic or CF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:280
#: f773cb0f2885432f98beb886d9cf94fb
msgid ""
"Often motors are \"charted\" with specific propellers and these are "
"certainly the best starting point for optimum performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:282
#: d3ac693380924993a94c349bd7e556ca
msgid ""
"TMotor is considered a premium prop, but good results have been obtained "
"with RC-Timer and Tarot in the large tapered props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:284
#: 7fe5a1c59309407da8cd6f2a17f4f9b0
msgid ""
"APC, DJI, GemFan, RC Drones and Graupner all produce good props in the "
"14\" and under category."
msgstr ""

