" or to center frame to avoid asymmetrical prop wash vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:559
#: b618021163484b0a926fe2d3ca1282e5
msgid ""
"A major design criteria is to size the frame appropriately for the "
"largest propellers you might ever want to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:561
#: 71d3a91f06d54f76a814f59b2c1887f2
msgid ""
"Generally bigger propeller diameter equals better efficiency and an X "
"frame layout normally permits the largest possible props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:564
#: 88a9ac57c8114819a8e2ed5bb5c0b3be
msgid ""
"Of course the motor speed and power and frame strength have to be matched"
" to the propeller diameter and to total lifting capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:567
#: d479fb81a69943f39d78e4c992b870e0
msgid "Pancake Low KV, Low RPM motors can turn bigger propellers efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:569
#: 1117759338ff4f29b7086b5529e9cc68
msgid ""
"It is possible to overlap prop tips if you have one above the other, but "
"it does affect efficiency and induces asymmetric vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:572
#: 3cad99a97ae644faae637abccf51e4ef
msgid ""
"Big slow props can have adverse vibration, instability, gust compensation"
" and response rate issues also so that is a downside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:576
#: 91367c30b7574f4c88e558d6d9dc3b53
msgid ""
"The additional motors of Hex and Octocopters can permit single motor out "
"recovery and provide for smoother flight for photo uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:579
#: 9bb0321fed7c40f7ab13f81b249214d7
msgid ""
"But they need to use smaller propellers because of motor to motor "
"clearance which is less efficient resulting in shorter flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:582
#: ba40780f74994828b3bfa464837a1b81
msgid ""
"There is also additional cost and weight of the frames and extra motors "
"and propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:584
#: aed3c458f5934b0289a2574ce67847e8
msgid "And, the overall increase in complexity also reduces reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:586
#: aa924e3da3a44662912ae5bc65535f09
msgid ""
"High quality extended service larger pancake motors and props are just "
"starting to become available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:588
#: 175192cb450242b98f7af16e583fcd3a
msgid ""
"So we are likely to see a shift to large Quadcopters from Hexacopters and"
" Octocopters even for professional and commercial uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:593
#: 73394ca41b43427589df9a2ddae4c351
msgid "The Carbon Fiber or Fiberglass Tube and Plate Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:595
#: fc7b0a6e8a6b47e7b0fffd42f99441c7
msgid ""
"The carbon fiber or fiberglass tube and plate frame is popular because it"
" is strong and light and easily manufactured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:598
#: 70e1a856e27e48978bfe36625b6f206e
msgid ""
"The `Tarot 650 <http://www.helipal.com/tarot-fy650-quadricopter-frame-"
"set.html>`__ is a typical layout medium sized carbon fiber Quadcopter "
"frame that can work with up to 17\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:602
#: bce01b39e53b4faead2305291a8c0681
msgid "It features folding arms and landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:603
#: 08fa66073c05490aac032793e056178c
msgid ""
"Its ability to support pancake motors and 17\" props means it can provide"
" long flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:605
#: dba3eb76ee5f42d7861a4d502706cf83
msgid ""
"Some people have said the quality of construction is not as good as it "
"could be but for $125.00 it is an amazing bargain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:611
#: 3d4c961a2e824c7e9f6459d994e87422
msgid ""
"Fabrication requirements and techniques for fiberglass and carbon fiber "
"tube and plate copters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:613
#: 3288714e48f84940927901eeccf89ce7
msgid ""
"On the copters shown above the method of attachment is by clamping carbon"
" fiber tube frame arms with aluminum brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:616
#: 5822b4c9eb8446ea8054179476d0897b
msgid ""
"This is because of the difficulties in attaching carbon fiber parts as "
"well as the stress that can result from drilling the tubing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:619
#: 0c25b21b83f24c0eb5f02a6be04ea061
msgid ""
"Fiberglass is not quite as strong or light as carbon fiber but it is more"
" flexible and easier to join and machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:622
#: 117818ee80e04c1388071cc6feae438f
msgid ""
"If what you need is available in a commercial frame kit you are normally "
"better off buying it as you will spend more making your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:625
#: 66d11cef05904cb5b21790c33332134c
msgid ""
"It will also take a lot of time and effort to design the copter, to "
"obtain the components and to, cut, drill, machine and fabricate them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:628
#: 130cad07439b4b57952cd1d63ecc04ba
msgid ""
"There is also a strong possibility that design and fabrication mistakes "
"and misperceptions will require that some things get redone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:632
#: 2e56d8747e1c420a9ddca118b6969c0b
msgid ""
"If you have sufficient reason to make your own frame, tube and plate "
"construction is generally the most practical for home production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:634
#: 0f8c005007cd4770a4d4e3f304d2d8f1
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to mix materials, commonly carbon fiber frame tubes and "
"fiberglass central and motor mounting plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:637
#: e31a08404d3f4a0fa6a5b2efcd6ae444
msgid ""
"Carbon fiber and fiberglass tubing and plate can be cut with a hacksaw or"
" power jig or band saw (with metal or fiberglass blades)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:641
#: 832962a98b634c9da2879a576bab19e1
msgid ""
"It can also be drilled and milled with HSS or TC coated drills and mills,"
" but all tooling wears out very quickly cutting these materials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:645
#: 17a7fe7df8fe414cb195985909c91b25
msgid ""
"Carbon fiber in particular is tricky to cut, drill and machine, it can "
"tear, shatter or de-laminate if not done smoothly and slowly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:648
#: d1f4512f907a41368426a7805d2be9fa
msgid ""
"A drill press is mandatory for carbon fiber, you cant center punch a "
"pilot drill hole, so it needs to be held precisely in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:651
#: b54c1f2ff8ee49249fbd93930508850d
msgid ""
"Avoid milling of carbon fiber if at all possible, it is very difficult to"
" accomplish satisfactory results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:653
#: e8616c31898c4cc99901888a67d3d121
msgid ""
"You will see carbon fiber plates that have milled slots on consumer "
"copters but these have generally been cut with a water jet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:656
#: e2af492b68ee44f5ad0ae57c570a00ab
msgid ""
"With carbon fiber you will generally get better results drilling "
"precision placed holes rather than attempting to mill slots in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:659
#: 1018b00a6de0466cb45f16b31d407cce
msgid ""
"You can carefully and slowly cut a carbon fiber plates exterior edges "
"with a power saw and smooth them with a Dremel tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:661
#: 3d5a4d9219654b999da88a7b5379ba05
msgid ""
"If you must put in slots consider drilling a hole at each end and using a"
" small circular saw on a Dremel or flex shaft to connect them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:665
#: 13975a2540cc49efb2ebe0888d4eb8b1
msgid ""
"It will be necessary to provide appropriate brackets to clamp the motor "
"mounts and central hub to the frame arm tubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:668
#: 2eab2696b0b445408a9afd7c84110b66
msgid ""
"Tubing needs to be clamped but must not be \"crushed\", silicone or "
"rubber gasket can provide protection and vibration isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:670
#: a4aa981aa0014286a86f404ecae75437
msgid ""
